{"schema":"symmetry-lab-pathways-provenance-1","release":"20261029-pathways1","date":"2026-10-29","originalContent":true,"scope":"Four bounded Python teaching workflows, original lessons/model presets and cross-module assignments, plus a context-aware read-only formula dictionary; no generic EBR, real-material fitting or thermodynamic phase claim","counts":{"modules":4,"lessons":14,"exercises":14,"cases":14,"exerciseSteps":56,"presets":26,"dictionaryEntries":66,"catalogSources":13,"dictionarySources":23,"sources":36,"uniqueSourceURLs":32,"projects":4,"retainedProjects":6,"projectCenterTotal":10},"projects":[{"id":"site-bloch-little-group","module":"bandrep","title":"from real space position to screw axis little group"},{"id":"bose-scattering","module":"scattering","title":"From resonator thermal occupation to both sides phonon Scattering"},{"id":"bulk-interface-localization","module":"domainwall","title":"From SSH bulk phase to interface localized state"},{"id":"hund-superexchange","module":"hubbard","title":"Distinguish between local Hund spin and inter-site super exchange"}],"models":[{"module":"band_rep_lab","coverage":["Site orbits, stabilizers, periodic-gauge Bloch matrices and selected-k little-group decomposition for ordinary space groups 2, 4, 19 and 221; scalar s or complete polar p orbitals"],"limitations":["BC primitive settings, including the group-4 screw along z; single-valued and no SOC/time reversal","No generic EBR classification, electronic energy calculation, structure identification or complete topological diagnosis"]},{"module":"dynamic_scattering_lab","coverage":["One-dimensional longitudinal diatomic harmonic chain with mass-normalized complex modes, coherent one-phonon amplitudes, Bose populations and positive/negative energy scattering"],"limitations":["Synthetic chain with explicit energy cutoff and relative scattering weights; no arbitrary Phonopy dataset import","No fitted material cross section, Debye-Waller factor, elastic/multiphonon scattering or computed damping"]},{"module":"domain_wall_lab","coverage":["Independent scalar phi4 pinned-wall finite-grid stationary calculation with continuum and Hessian diagnostics","Independent finite open SSH chain with central-pair potential, LDOS and selected-subspace spatial projectors"],"limitations":["Reduced continuum units do not automatically map to SSH parameters or fitted ferroelectric energies","Finite-grid residual is distinct from unconstrained stability; spatial windows may overlap and finite chains need not reach asymptotic dimerization"]},{"module":"hubbard_lab","coverage":["Exact fermionic diagonalization of 2-4 site open/periodic single-band Hubbard clusters in fixed up/down particle sectors","Degenerate-ground-state trace averages, densities, double occupancy, spin correlations, U scans, all-Sz charge gaps and dimer singlet-triplet splitting"],"limitations":["Two-site periodic model has one undirected bond; zero temperature and supplied model parameters","Finite-sector gaps and finite-cluster charge costs do not prove a thermodynamic Mott transition or material magnetic order"]}],"dictionaryScope":"Definitions, variables, units and conventions are selected using route/formula context; unresolved ambiguity and unknown formulas are not guessed, and original source math is preserved.","sources":[{"id":"bandrep-cano-ebr","title":"Cano et al., Building Blocks of Topological Quantum Chemistry: Elementary Band Representations, PRB 97, 035139 (2018)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.01935"},{"id":"bandrep-elcoro-bcs","title":"Elcoro et al., Double crystallographic groups and their representations on the Bilbao Crystallographic Server, J. Appl. Cryst. 50, 1457–1477 (2017)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.09272"},{"id":"bandrep-bilbao-sitesym","title":"Bilbao Crystallographic Server: SiteSym site-symmetry induction method","url":"https://cryst.ehu.eus/html/rep/sitesym/sitesym_help.html"},{"id":"bandrep-spglib-dataset","title":"spglib official documentation: symmetry dataset and Wyckoff positions","url":"https://spglib.readthedocs.io/en/stable/dataset.html"},{"id":"scattering-scattering-phonopy-dsf","title":"Phonopy: coherent one-phonon dynamic structure factor and phase conventions","url":"https://phonopy.github.io/phonopy/dynamic-structure-factor.html"},{"id":"scattering-scattering-phonopy-formulation","title":"Phonopy: dynamical matrix and displacement eigenvectors","url":"https://phonopy.github.io/phonopy/formulation.html#dynamical-matrix"},{"id":"scattering-scattering-togo-2023","title":"Togo, Chaput, Tadano & Tanaka, Implementation strategies in phonopy and phono3py (2023)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.05784"},{"id":"domainwall-tong","title":"David Tong · Statistical Field Theory: domain walls","url":"https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/sft/one.pdf"},{"id":"domainwall-ssh","title":"Su, Schrieffer, Heeger (1979), Solitons in Polyacetylene","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.42.1698"},{"id":"domainwall-asboth","title":"Asbóth, Oroszlány, Pályi · A Short Course on Topological Insulators","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.02295"},{"id":"hubbard-hubbard-original","title":"J. Hubbard, Electron correlations in narrow energy bands, Proc. R. Soc. Lond. A 276, 238–257 (1963)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1963.0204"},{"id":"hubbard-hubbard-dimer","title":"D. J. Carrascal et al., The Hubbard Dimer: A density functional case study of a many-body problem, J. Phys.: Condens. Matter 27, 393001 (2015)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1502.02194"},{"id":"hubbard-hubbard-lieb-wu","title":"E. H. Lieb and F. Y. Wu, Absence of Mott Transition in an Exact Solution of the Short-Range, One-Band Model in One Dimension, Phys. Rev. Lett. 20, 1445–1448 (1968)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.20.1445"},{"id":"dictionary-iucr-hm","title":"IUCr：Hermann–Mauguin symbols","url":"https://dictionary.iucr.org/Hermann-Mauguin_symbols"},{"id":"dictionary-bilbao","title":"Bilbao Crystallographic Server: Representati